marked, two-sided p = 0.0414) and rejects the no-preference null, treating each row as an independent Bernoulli trial even though the rows are four repeated tests per colony sharing the same nest, forager pool, and pheromone-extract batch.\",\"The analysis n (20 trials) exceeds the number of independent units (5 colonies) by a factor of four, and within-colony correlation is visible in the data (COL-01 and COL-02 chose the marked arm in all 8 of their trials while COL-05 chose it in only 1 of 4), so the reported significance rests on an inflated effective sample size; the issue is therefore demonstrated in the selected report.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["The declared independent-unit column colony_id is consistent with the frozen data: the column exists in data/input.csv, contains COL-01 through COL-05, and each colony contributes exactly four rows as the data description states, with both outcome arms (marked/plain) represented across those grouped rows.","The selected report pools all 20 rows into scipy.stats.binomtest (15 of 20 marked, two-sided p = 0.0414) and rejects the no-preference null, treating each row as an independent Bernoulli trial even though the rows are four repeated tests per colony sharing the same nest, forager pool, and pheromone-extract batch.","The analysis n (20 trials) exceeds the number of independent units (5 colonies) by a factor of four, and within-colony correlation is visible in the data (COL-01 and COL-02 chose the marked arm in all 8 of their trials while COL-05 chose it in only 1 of 4), so the reported significance rests on an inflated effective sample size; the issue is therefore demonstrated in the selected report.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms"